WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.170
- What's up, everybody!

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.880
We are back with Megan Fox!

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.865
Give it up!

00:00:03.865 --> 00:00:04.970
(audience cheers)

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.260
The month of May means
a lot of great things.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.330
Flowers are in bloom.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.050
Summer is around the corner.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.300
School is almost out for your kids,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.720
all you mamas and daddies out there.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.740
And each year we take Memorial Day

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.500
to honor those who have given their lives

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.170
serving in our military.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.840
This is something very important to Megan

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.960
which is why she's partnered

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.240
with army combat veteran, Colin Wayne.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.970
So Colin is joining us now.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.970
Thank you for joining us
(applause)

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.940
and thank you so much for your service.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.030
It seems so silly and
such a little thing to say

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.260
for you giving so much,

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.770
but thank you.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.020
We really do appreciate it.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.760
And I'm curious how you two even met

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.260
and how this all happened.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.970
- You reached out to me.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.803
- Yeah.

00:00:42.803 --> 00:00:45.160
- Reached out from far away.
- Not from over there.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.980
About the products and the
business that you have.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.430
And so I had collaborated
with him once before.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.900
I have veterans in my family.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.720
My uncles are all vets.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.620
But you should tell more.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.810
I'm assuming it probably has something

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.560
to do with the fact that like,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.740
the Transformers movies, especially,

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.690
Michael especially is very pro-military,

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.900
very supportive of the military.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.580
And those movies reached out

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.080
and featured a lot of military

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.570
and were very inclusive in that way.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.403
So I imagine,

00:01:14.297 --> 00:01:16.840
I might have a small
voice in that community

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:17.910
or be able to help them out.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.640
- And also you're a big, huge star

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.680
that people pay attention to.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.640
That's maybe one, too.
(laughing)

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.780
I'll say that for you.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.950
But how did you end up hooking up?

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.200
- Well, we wanted to
partner with somebody,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.790
you mentioned a small voice,

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.300
but your voice is magnified.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.473
It's massive.

00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:35.050
And we know that

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.550
went overseas to Korea

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.490
and visited the troops.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.380
I did three tours:

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.070
Egypt, Iraq, and Afghanistan.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.110
And so when we were looking for somebody

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.410
to kind of spread the
message and the awareness

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.300
of what Memorial Day
even is to begin with,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.960
because it's been lost in this nation

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.043
of the true meaning,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.010
it was a clear understanding

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.360
that this could be a great fit

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.200
and it has been.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.170
This is our second year doing it

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.330
and it's been an honor.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.020
I know last year we donated

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.250
over two and a half million
dollars in products.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.720
- Wow, that's amazing.
- [Megan] Yeah.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.900
- So, I have to ask you,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.540
'cause I always ask anybody
that served their country,

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.130
what drew you to serving our country?

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.690
- So, like a lot of people
I grew up in a split home,

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.564
just like you Kelly.
- Me too. Mmhmm.

00:02:19.564 --> 00:02:22.053
And my mom primarily raised me and

00:02:23.138 --> 00:02:25.530
I didn't have a difficult childhood

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.280
but I had an older brother
that I looked up to

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.760
as a father figure.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.860
He joined the military at 17

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.330
and I ended up getting kicked

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.180
out of my mom's house.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.230
I wasn't a bad kid, but
I was stubborn by nature.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.750
And I just wouldn't listen to her.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.480
So I dropped out of high school at 16,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.740
joined the military at 17,
after getting emancipated

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.190
and went as a military police officer

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.150
and made staff sergeant in six years.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.440
So, I was one of the
youngest staff sergeants

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.470
in the army without being Special Forces

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.020
and actually volunteered
for all three of my tours.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.410
So Egypt, Iraq, and Afghanistan.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.800
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.710
Well, something happened
on your last tour.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:04.930
What was it?

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.290
- So, I remember it like it was yesterday

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.120
which ironically was just a few days ago.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.190
Nine years ago I was in Afghanistan

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.360
in the Paktika province

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.360
which is right on the Pakistan border.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.370
And a rocket impacted

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.070
about three and a half feet from me.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.090
And through the grace of God, I survived.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.410
Shrapnel went all the way through my leg.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.110
I remember I blacked out,

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.180
I regained consciousness and...

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.330
it was,

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.483
I couldn't see my hand
in front of my face.

00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:37.330
I was yelling for a medic

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.180
but nobody was coming
and it felt like eternity

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.380
but really it was only a few minutes.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.060
I remember it was just like
a movie set, but it was true.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.320
Two Blackhawks came in, picked me up.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.210
I was the only casualty.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.200
They flew me to another base and...

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.120
I ended up sustaining shrapnel

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.500
to both arms,

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.970
a piece went all the way through my leg

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.440
and almost had to have it amputated.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.210
Treated for traumatic brain injury

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.410
and then L1-L3 nerve damage in my back.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.420
So, I had to have a lumbar
block fusion surgery.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.870
- Wow. So, how do you

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.190
not only recover from that physically,

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.490
but like emotionally and mentally?

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.190
- So, ironically,

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.470
I started working out in 2009,

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.970
right before I started to go
to Iraq for my second tour.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.730
And I...

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.180
the gym was my real focal point.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.290
It helped me,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.910
that mind, body connection.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.180
Ironically, I got blown up in a gym

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.210
on my base that I thought
was a safe harbor,

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.523
but the gym helped me cope
with a lot of things mentally.

00:04:46.089 --> 00:04:48.870
And I say ironic several
times because I pivoted

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:52.350
from the military into
becoming a fitness model.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.620
And that setback was
a setup for my future.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.228
- Wow. I need to write
that down for myself.

00:04:58.228 --> 00:04:59.310
(laughing)

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.110
So, you've partnered

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.810
to do something special for Memorial day.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.250
So what is it?

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.470
- So, this year I'm honored

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.730
for our second annual
soldier memorial give back.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.960
Last year we had an incredible response

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.500
and we had the privilege to donate

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.160
over two and a half a million
dollars worth of product.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.640
- [Kelly] That's so great.
- And this year we plan

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.830
to do the same

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.540
with a minimum of a million dollars.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.280
Anytime I put my name behind something

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.340
I want it to be a hundred percent.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.560
For me it's important that Memorial Day

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.800
is a day to honor,

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.320
not me as a veteran,

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:35.380
but to those that paid
the ultimate sacrifice.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:38.250
Nine years ago that could
have been me that got killed.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:42.990
And fortunately, I'm here to
be a voice for the voiceless.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.310
- [Kelly] Yeah.
I'm here to be a voice

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.770
for the family members
that lost their loved ones.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.530
So their sons, their
daughters, their husbands,

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.480
their moms, their dads.
(applause)

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:56.400
It's important to me as an entrepreneur,

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.740
as a veteran

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:01.090
to be a hands extended and to be a voice

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.530
for those that simply do not have a voice

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.960
anymore.
- Yeah.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:06.830
Well, two questions.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.240
Can you tell us about your company?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.690
one, and then two,

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.950
how can people help?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.870
What is, if people are
really wanting to help,

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:14.780
what can they do?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:19.240
- So, 2016, I founded
a company Redline Steel

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:21.423
and we manufacturer wall art decor.

00:06:22.331 --> 00:06:25.400
The piece that we're
actually donating for free

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.230
is a really beautiful

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.440
nine inch steel sign

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.833
that we're literally just
giving away for free.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.153
The meaning behind it is,

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.720
fallen comrades in active line of service

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.840
from Iraq to Afghanistan,

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.020
this soldier Memorial represents them.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.180
And so this is a remembrance piece.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:53.180
Nowadays, Memorial Day is
known for companies monetizing.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.320
- [Kelly] Oh sales, yeah.
- You look at social media

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.550
across the board.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.310
You look at car sales

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.080
or buy this mattress "Memorial Day sale."

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.950
This is the opposite.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.900
We want to put people over profit.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.340
We want to truly spread the message

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.230
and hopefully have a third annual

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.080
and fourth annual Memorial Day give back.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.320
It's not about just me as a veteran.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.640
It's not about anything other than

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.240
the family members that
lost their loved ones.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.073
- I agree with you.

00:07:24.073 --> 00:07:26.020
I think people have lost sight of that.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.750
Well, thank you so much
for your service once again

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.840
and thank y'all for teaming up.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:30.840
This is really cool.

